    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I changed to satisfy the spec with low structural impact:\n\n**Behaviour**\n- `membershipLevel` is now a numeric field (1\u20133): starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). The string `membershipTier` and the household-based `GOLD` override are gone.\n\n**Changes**\n1. `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` string property with an integer `membershipLevel` (min 1, max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the new field.\n2. **New** `MembershipLevel.java` \u2014 a small cohesive helper (`of(Owner)`) that computes the level; the single home for the rule, mirroring the old `HouseholdTier` shape.\n3. `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one-line mapping change: `membershipTier` expression \u2192 `membershipLevel` via `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, so every response path derives it uniformly.\n4. `LogAuditOnCreate.java` \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel=\u2026` instead of nothing tier-related (verified in the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 \u2026 membershipLevel=3`).\n5. `RespondWithOwner.java` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 removed the obsolete `HouseholdTier.applyTo` call (GOLD override no longer exists).\n6. Deleted `HouseholdTier.java` (dead once the tier field was removed).\n\nEach touched function stayed CC-1 and the new logic lives in a fresh, low-complexity unit rather than being grown into an existing class. `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
